![Content Overview panel (develop), light theme — visual reference](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

### What differs between the two versions

Develop (merged, PR 244 lineage) — comment here to defend or challenge any of these choices:

- Consumes Weft primitives: `Button`, `Badge`, `Collapsible` section/group headers.
- Shows a `Read only` permission badge when the viewer lacks write access.
- Dedicated empty state: `This space has no browsable content yet.`
- Dedicated auth-error state: `Runtime auth required` / `Content Overview unavailable`.
- Wraps the panel as `section` with `aria-label="Content Overview"`; collapse state via `CollapsibleTrigger` + `aria-expanded`.

Stale branch nod-978 (PR 242, closed) — choices that did NOT survive the merge:

- Full ARIA tree semantics: `role="tree"` on the list, `role="treeitem"` + `aria-expanded` on sections, groups, and items — richer screen-reader navigation than the merged Collapsible approach.
- Raw `<button>` section/group headers instead of Weft `CollapsibleTrigger`.
- `main` landmark instead of labeled `section`.
- Direct Clerk `getToken` wiring instead of the shared `authSnapshot` runtime-auth path.

Open reconciliation question for the design-system example: should the merged panel re-adopt the branch's `role="tree"` semantics on top of the Weft collapsible primitives? Comment on this line with the call.

