### Version A — board as merged to `develop`

- Renders with the reviewed comp's pinned dark palette regardless of app theme (the demo scope CSS pins it; the board does not yet resolve the live Weft theme).
- Rail presets (`Updated since` / `Due` / `Assigned to`) render but are display-level; structured preset state lands in PR 496.

![Updates Dashboard board — develop merged state (comp-pinned palette)](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

### Version B — PR 496 (`claude/updates-dashboard-board-surface`, NOD-1254)

Comment on any line to endorse or challenge it:

- **Theme-following board through the product mount** — the board resolves the real Weft theme; light and dark below.
- Structured rail filters wired as state: `Updated since` presets (any date / past 24h / past 7 days / past 30 days), `Due` presets (any time / overdue / next 7 days), `Assignee` (anyone / actor) — client-side narrowing over already-loaded canonical rows, never a refetch.
- Canonical `spaceId` identity for filtering and dedup — duplicate space display names can no longer cross-contaminate rows.
- Row provenance: rows carry `source: aggregate | related`; related rows keep relation evidence (kind label such as `search_hit`, plus the project they relate to); provenance is never invented downstream.
- Degradation notice for answered-but-partial spaces (truncated / one list failed) — reported separately from failed spaces, never counted as a failure.
- Preview drawers gain canonical ids and body excerpts; panel variant gains a compact context subtitle.
- Scale: 4,651 insertions across 24 files vs develop, including a 311-line board controller state.

![Updates Dashboard board — PR 496 theme-following, light theme](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

![Updates Dashboard board — PR 496 theme-following, dark theme](data:image/jpeg;base64,)


### Version B, verified live (fixture mode, captured 2026-07-29)

Ran from the branch per Aaron's reference notes — no node or auth needed:

- Worktree of `claude/updates-dashboard-board-surface`; private weft dep installed via a temp npmrc (`//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=$(gh auth token)` + `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` install).
- `npm run dev -- --port 5199`; surfaces: `/updates-dashboard-demo` (comp + live parity, the dark zero-diff gate target), `/?heddle-demo-mocks=1` (widget in real workspace slots: wide board in a wide slot, compact panel in a narrow one), `/updates-dashboard-live` (loader error states without a node).
- Theme-following confirmed live: the board resolves Weft Light / Weft Dark from the app theme (Settings → Theme in the workspace; theme contract attributes in the demo).

**Compact panel variant** (`panel` view, 258px) — the narrow-slot rendering of the same widget. Anatomy, each line commentable:

- Panel header: `Updates Dashboard · panel`
- Search input: `Search projects · all spaces`
- Heading: `All open action items` · caption `across 4 spaces · no search term`
- Summary row: `Blockers · act now` — count 1 (red dot)
- Summary row: `Awaiting you` — count 4 (amber dot)
- Summary row: `FYI · worth knowing` — count 3 (blue dot)

![Updates Dashboard compact panel (258px), light theme](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Signal drawer** (`drawer-signal` view, 480px) — opened from a board row. Anatomy, each line commentable:

- Chips: type `signal` · state `blocked · 5d`
- Title: `Account Recovery dependency unresolved`
- Meta: `Opened 5d ago · assigned to A. Steele · Nodaste Studio`
- Canonical id with Copy affordance: `nodaste-studio/heddle-ui/sig_4c2a3f9e`
- Body: `The account-recovery flow depends on the ccore/heddle token migration, which isn't merged yet. It blocks shipping the board's ok/stop status colors.`
- Reply affordance: `Reply...`
- Provenance line: `Why you're seeing this:` `direct id` chip · `tagged to Heddle UI (pr_9f2a...c1)` — the never-invented provenance rule, made visible
- Action row: `Resolve for me` (primary) · `Reassign` · `Open in C-Core`

![Signal drawer (480px), light theme](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Live loader error states** (`/updates-dashboard-live`, no node running) — both the wide board and compact panel degrade to the same recoverable shape:

- Error callout: `Couldn't load action items.` `Connecting your account...`
- Recovery affordance: `Retry`

![Board and panel loader error states without a node, light theme](data:image/jpeg;base64,)

**Weft touchpoints in this branch** — each line is a token-governance point; comment to accept or push back:

- `updatesDashboardCompSource.html` is the single source of truth for the board treatment; `scripts/generate-updates-dashboard-comp.mjs` emits both the comp and `updatesDashboardBoardTreatment.generated.ts` from it, with a `--check` drift gate.
- `BoardTreatment.tsx` mounts the treatment; mock-only deltas are scoped strictly under `:root[data-theme='dark']`; light derives purely from `--weft-*` tokens.
- The bridge's `!important` serif promotion on h1–h3 is countered with a scoped sans override (same convention as work-board).
- Dark `--weft-link` is `#5b87fd` as of weft 0.2.1 — the board consumes it as-is.
- The brighter ok/stop greens in the dark treatment are **mock-scoped deltas, not canonical tokens** — the open "green-400" thread in the weft repo decides whether they graduate. Comment here with the token call.
- Committed light/dark baselines: `tests/visual/updates-dashboard-states.spec.ts`.

Adjacent but separate: `codex_updates_dashboard_verification` (your current heddle checkout) iterates on Working Threads actor-identity attribution; it is not a board candidate but its identity-tuple rules overlap PR 496's `spaceId`/provenance work — worth one reconciliation pass so the two don't define identity differently. Comment here if that pass should be its own ticket.

